==============================================================================
(1) KILL-A -- THE T-LAW DECOUPLING PROGRAM
==============================================================================
  TEST  : r_T on r_R in the SAME systems; coupled null r_T = 2 r_R (T ~ v^2, SAME sigma^2)
  SAMPLE: 55 HI dwarfs (G114, rms 0.150 dex -- the RAR-holds anchor)
          + 12 X-COP + 12 HeCS-with-T = 24 cluster systems with BOTH kT and sigma_dyn
  ERRORS: sig_T pooled 0.109 dex (3-sig = 0.326 dex; X-COP 0.051 / HeCS 0.178 / E11 0.083)
          sig_R 0.150 dex (G114), 0.053 dex HSE (X-COP)
  POWER : the shared M_b/a0 offset shows the r_T-r_R correlation at >= 3 sig with power 0.8 at N = 17-25; power 0.77 at N = 24
          mean-offset: N(delta 0.15 dex) = 5, N(delta 0.10) = 11, single-pair 0.326 dex
  KILL  : slope-0 consistent at > 3 sig, OR a single pair |r_T| > 0.326 dex against a holding RAR
  DATE  : re-reduction TODAY (data on the record); HeCS-without-T 46 closes via eRASS1

==============================================================================
(2) KILL-B -- THE MASS DECOUPLING PROGRAM
==============================================================================
  LADDER: m = 5.089 +- 0.097 keV, 3-sig band [4.798, 5.379] keV
  LINE  : E = m/2 = 2.5443 keV in [2.50, 2.60], sigma_E 1.19 eV (FWHM 2.80), envelope [2.80, 19.03] eV
